SUMMARY:Aiko Shimada Jazz Quintet Live @ The Melon Ball
DESCRIPTION:Watermelon Music in Davis presents Aiko Shimada Jazz Quintet. \nAiko Shimada is a Sacramento-based jazz vocalist known for a warm\, ethereal tone and an honest\, restrained approach to interpretation. \nOnce a singer-guitarist/songwriter who performed and toured widely for decades in Seattle\, she now returns to jazz\, blending beloved standards with originals and thoughtful covers. \nNotable collaborators include the late world-renowned pianist Jessica Williams\, and acclaimed jazz guitarist Bill Frisell appears on her album Blue Marble (John Zorn’s Tzadik Label in New York). \nJoined by Selena Delgadillo (piano)\, Mark Collins (upright bass)\, Stephen Esquivido (sax)\, and Aidan Smith (drums)\, Aiko offers an evening of elegance\, intimacy\, and sincerity shaped by influences from Billie Holiday and Shirley Horn to Thelonious Monk\, Miles Davis\, Cassandra Wilson\, Egberto Gismonti\, and Brazilian singer Mônica Salmaso. \nPress \n“Stunning live” — The Stranger\, Seattle\n“Beautiful\, profound\, and original… haunting\, mature\, unforgettable.” — Steve Silberman\, Wired\n“Shimada is one of the most original and creative musicians on the Seattle scene.” — Seattle Times\n“Her music is a fluid and exquisitely ear-friendly blend of lower Manhattan jazz and textural forms…” — Sacramento News & Review \nInstagram: @aikoshimada.music\nYouTube: Aiko Shimada Music & Beyond \nThis is a BOYB show!  Watermelon Music serves non-alcoholic drinks and pre-packaged snacks. \n$15 General Admission\n$10 Students (available in-store or at the door only)\nKids under 12 are FREE!
URL:https://visityolo.com/event/aiko-shimada-jazz-quintet-live-the-melon-ball/
LOCATION:Watermelon Music\, 1970 Lake Blvd\, DAVIS\, CA\, 95616\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visityolo.com/wp-content/uploads/061326TICKET_Rev-1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Watermelon Music":MAILTO:info@watermelonmusic.com
END:VEVENT
